*To track it here,* archival criteria is i) not using account for 6 months (or less/more depending on the market); ii ) not confirming the email address when logging into (depending on the market).

{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}
This makes the risk lower in terms of unauthorised access to the user’s accounts, but it still presents a risk and we will not recommend proceeding with this as we anticipate a lot of incidents here.
{panel}



So, to summarise, *we have to decide from the business side on one of the short-term solutions:*

* *S1*: Archive the existing account with matching phone number *only* when it meets archival criteria. Otherwise we give user a choice to switch to the existing account or continue with current account (in this case existing account will be archived). 
** *Privacy Risk:* {color:#bf2600}*HIGH*{color}
** *Probability* of unauthorised access to another user account is {color:#bf2600}*HIGH*{color}
* *S2:* Archive the existing account with matching phone number always. Do not give user a choice to log in to the existing account and ask to continue with current account.
** *Privacy Risk:* {color:#ff991f}*MEDIUM (as users will not be able to use/access their personal data any longer, while there is no risk of unauthorised access)*{color}
** *Probability* of unauthorised access to another user account is {color:#006644}*LOW*{color}

