What should be done: we should add period connection cleanup to {{DbPool}}.

* There’s already an intervalic cleanup happening in {{triggerConnectionToCleanUpPoolIfNeeded}}: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/blob/cf7b4ef6f1ebd42607970ed5b3dd1be00da92acf/src/async/db/DbPool.ts#L271-L291|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/blob/cf7b4ef6f1ebd42607970ed5b3dd1be00da92acf/src/async/db/DbPool.ts#L271-L291]
However, this code is related to the logic which is keeping the pool size under 10 connections if possible. The new logic could be in the same method or separately. Just make sure that two pieces of logic are not conflicting.
* The simplest way would be to iterate over all connections and purge all of the “old” ones (checked via {{shouldPurgeActiveConnectionByMaxTime}}). The problem is that there’s no clear API to iterate through connections. Maybe it’s possible to access the native pool’s private properties, since we’re already doing it for some other purposes.
* An alternative would be to implement a simple check like this:
{noformat}if (freeConnectionsAvailable) {
    const connection = await getConnection();
    if (isOld(connection)) {
        connection.purge();
    }
}{noformat}
This should eventually remove all of the old connections, since native pool uses round robin to cycle through connections, so eventually all connections will be iterated through, unless they are destroyed earlier: [https://github.com/mysqljs/mysql#pooling-connections:~:text=Connections%20are%20also%20cycled%20round%2Drobin%20style%2C%20with%20connections%20being%20taken%20from%20the%20top%20of%20the%20pool%20and%20returning%20to%20the%20bottom.|https://github.com/mysqljs/mysql#pooling-connections:~:text=Connections%20are%20also%20cycled%20round%2Drobin%20style%2C%20with%20connections%20being%20taken%20from%20the%20top%20of%20the%20pool%20and%20returning%20to%20the%20bottom.|smart-link] For more detailed justification of why it should work check the following message in {{#dev-pint}}: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C046TK6FZ7Z/p1729760707555749?thread_ts=1726139576.777419&cid=C046TK6FZ7Z|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C046TK6FZ7Z/p1729760707555749?thread_ts=1726139576.777419&cid=C046TK6FZ7Z|smart-link] I’ve also attached the same diagram below.
