Hi [~accountid:63622ea17d4645af4f03bd18] - As discussed, revised draft to the ICO is below, to which we can attach the screenshot I sent you.

In response to your queries:

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
* Appropriate steps are taken to address this with the driver in question. - {{think this is covered by the response to user but did we actually reach out to the driver?}}
{panel}

On the same day as the incident (1 June), Bolt Safety Team [reached out|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/385856585] to the driver saying “_We received a report from the driver that stated that you allegedly tried contacting and yelling at the passenger after the ride. We would like to believe that this is not a common occurrence and it was simply a misunderstanding. However, this report, while inconclusive at this time, may be used as a reference in the future should something similar occur again. This is not to assume guilt, but just for safety precautions_”. This effectively closed the issue on the driver side.

This falls short of telling the driver to not contact other users in relation to complaints, however it could at least be interpreted as a warning. I have reached out to the CS team to see if it would be viable to send a follow-up to the driver to remind them to refrain from doing this sort of thing, but I will leave it up to the relevant teams regarding whether this is an approach we should take. As such, I do not think this affects the drafting of the ICO response. 

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
* Procedures are in place to limit access to customers personal data to individuals that have a business need to access it.- {{think this is covered by the response to user}}
{panel}

Agreed.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
* All staff and drivers are aware of their obligations to use the personal data they have access to appropriately. - {{we should probably update response to ICO to make reference to our T&Cs/Privacy Notice}}
