Hello Team,

Regarding the rider’s blocking we suggest a slight adjustment in the terms and conditions.

We would need to take in mind the following:

* we will always need to ensure the rider the right to appeal of the suspension/blocking decision and expose the right to take legal action;
* we will need to make a pre-warning, like “if this misconduct happens again you may be suspended or blocked of using Bolt services.“
* to justify the suspension/blocking the behaviour needs to be reiterated;
* we need to understand that the blocking itself is in other terms a termination of the contract. Therefore, to be valid, the behaviour should affect Bolt and its services/should be a serious case.
* there is nothing in consumer law that does not allow the act of suspend/block users.
* TVDE Law determines in article 8 (1) - TVDE services may only be refused if they: b) Are requested by people with suspiciously dangerous behaviour;

Please have a look and confirm if these scenarios cover all the situations being considered:



