Hey! The novelty here would be related to the fact that Cargoson would act only as the connection enabler, meaning a same ride would be the object of different agreements with: 
(i) a Business customer, and 
(ii) Cargoson. 

_By default we’d contract directly only with an API integration partner (here: Cargoson) so that rides could be requested from Bolt platform over the API. We’d cover also all the billing, payment collection etc with such API partner and then the partner would manage everything with their 3rd party partners (“demand partners”) on their side._

If instead here we were to separate the rights and obligations of the API integration partner and leave some of these with a “demand partner” (and treat the latter as our regular Bolt Business customer) then we’d need to ensure that it was clear who’s responsible for what and that there weren’t any loopholes with regards to liability etc.

[~accountid:60b2030ffe01e80069c64f5f] [~accountid:712020:80adc2a7-05ca-4e9d-b299-6ace53125c4f] please consider it would be a non standard RB API arrangement while the wider organization (especially also Commerce, Finance) is necessarily not aligned on how RB API should function in the first place in order for it to be compliant (included in the Q4 MVRA), but leaving my 2 cents from the contractual end below. Assuming all what is suggested is doable technically, e.g. not sure I’m following the bit about _“hierarchy would be individual business accounts for each client, and individual Ride Booker account connected to the Business Accounts, accessed only by Cargoson”_. Could you please elaborate on the exact technical setup here?

+Agreement with a Business customer+

That should principally work _as is_ based on the [Business General T&Cs|https://bolt.eu/et-ee/legal/terms-for-bolt-business/?category=boltBusiness] and [special terms|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wT9xRPC07hAYnFUd7RJV-dwXf2wb5qk5vdEParroo9U/edit?tab=t.0] however I’d elaborate in the latter how the ride requests are technically made over an API (e.g. edits to the definitions of Bolt Business and Bolt Services), and specify the role and liability of Cargoson in this. Especially if Cargoson was granted access to customer’s account in any way - it must become clear for the customer so that they could consider this also in their agreement with Cargoson if and as needed. Bolt should obviously steer clear of any liability in this regard.

The billing and payments per standard contractual clauses in the special terms (not involving Cargoson).

+Agreement with API integration partner (Cargoson)+

Compared to our [template|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BS8VUWyJekCexkDFTAKopqNeYu1QvPwUMR8NdW2b5-0/edit?tab=t.0] [didn’t want to overload the [Cargoson draft|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FHQ7b5svT1ZiU5VRtZrImvKVKgj5H9-3/edit] with redline at this point] we’d need to specify or remove irrelevant clauses, incl 

* 1.2-1-4 Definitions - if unlike other RB API partnerships here there wouldn’t be any users in play who’d factually request a ride (in their native app) but instead it’s always customer reps via Cargoson software then the relevant def’s to be adjusted; Also to be checked if we can/should specify that ride requests under this arrangement are limited only to Bolt Send;
* 2.1 - possibly tone to be adjusted so that 3rd party partners weren’t considered as Cargoson’s partners but separately customers of both Cargoson and Bolt;
* 2.3 - questionable if Cargoson would accept taking up liability for the Business customers;
* 2.7, 5 - Equally we should make clear that Cargoson remains liable for all its activity under customer’s account;
* 2.10 - to be edited based on the specifics of this arrangement;
* 3 - to be removed in full. Possibly an informative clause or two to elaborate how all payments happen between Bolt and a customer, and between Cargoson and a customer respectively; and how each party will be remunerated by the customer for enabling this API connection (if applicable);
* 5.2 - reference to payments to be removed; also a fixed amount should be reflected as the liability gap as the are no regular payments between Cargoson and Bolt;
* 5.4 - Cargoson not liable for User activity;
* 6 - needs to be ensured termination regime is aligned with the one we agree with each customer;
* annex 1 - doesn’t harm to keep, but last sentence of clause 3 might remain relevant.

