Summary of problem, using default REPEATABLE-READ gives different results in TiDB vs MySQL:


{noformat}TIDB

t1: START TRANSACTION;

t2: START TRANSACTION; 

t1: SELECT vendor_id, latest_version_no, id as menu_id FROM vendor_menu WHERE vendor_id=1 FOR UPDATE;

t2: ## this blocks waiting on t1 to commit/rollback
SELECT vendor_id, latest_version_no, id as menu_id FROM vendor_menu WHERE vendor_id=1 FOR UPDATE;  ## blocks

t1: INSERT INTO `menu_item_data` ....
t1: SELECT * FROM menu_item_data; ## sees own inserted data

t2: still blocked 

t1: COMMIT;

t2: unblocks and returns data on vendor_menu table (WAS BLOCKED ON FOR UPDATE)

t2: SELECT * FROM menu_item_data; ## sees no data/empty table, snapshot isolation/repeatable read{noformat}

VS

{noformat}MYSQL 

t1: START TRANSACTION;

t2: START TRANSACTION; 

t1: SELECT vendor_id, latest_version_no, id as menu_id FROM vendor_menu WHERE vendor_id=1 FOR UPDATE;

t2: ## this blocks waiting on t1 to commit/rollback
SELECT vendor_id, latest_version_no, id as menu_id FROM vendor_menu WHERE vendor_id=1 FOR UPDATE;  ## blocks

t1: INSERT INTO `menu_item_data` ....
t1: SELECT * FROM menu_item_data; ## sees own data

t2: still blocked 

t1: COMMIT;

t2: unblocks and returns data on vendor_menu table (WAS BLOCKED ON FOR UPDATE)
t2: SELECT * FROM menu_item_data; ## sees data inserted in t1 (line 12){noformat}

