* If Bolt receives an allegation that the passenger has acted in an inappropriate way towards a driver, or if a passenger has physically assaulted a driver the customer service team will open up an investigation and will contact both the driver and the passenger to gather further information about the incident. 
* Customer service contacts the passenger and gives them 24hrs to respond, if the passenger does not respond within this timeframe a reminder message is sent, if the passenger still fails to provide a response the investigation will be closed and a decision will be made based on the evidence that CS have gathered. 
* When the CS team go to contact the passenger in some instances there may be multiple accounts with the same/similar email address. [~accountid:5ed4b18fc3b5390c24a6f905] and [~accountid:60dc82b73136170077b67c53] want to know if they are able to the send the email to all off the accounts. {color:#ff5630}- seek advice from Privacy Legal Team. {color}
* At the moment the CS team are sending the message on Beehive to one account and waiting to see if the passenger responds, then they proceed with the block. However, the CS team want to know if they are able to send the message to all of the accounts (for example if one email address is attached to 3 different accounts), they would like to know if this is possible or if this would have any risks involved by creating confusion (in case it is a different user). 

